{"text":"I want to implement a little bit more structure in the way I'm using these LLMs through my Droid plugin. Essentially, what I want to do is to have my buffer be able to have a multi-turn conversation with the model. And so, right now, the plugin really only just works for one-shotting problems, but I'd like to be able to have separate like user-assistant pairs. And so, I've attached, like, right, I've attached my entire NeoGham configuration, but really just focus on droid.lua. I've also provided an example of how I think a conversation ought to look like. It would be like some beginning and demarcation marks for the assistant messages, and then the rest of it is considered user message, and then you can like parse it out. There are like this assumes I keep everything like properly structured. I'm like, I ought to consider what happens in cases where, say, for example, I don't have any text between two assistant responses. Maybe I change something. So, like, in those cases, although I don't think that would necessarily be likely, but regardless, there should just be some clean error handling there just to make sure we have actual message pairs. I don't think we need to do like a crazy internal deciphering to parse them. I think we throw in a clean error with like mini notify and call it a day. But yeah, this is like the first layer. How do you think I should implement this? How do you think I should like handle the parsing, those demarcations? Like, how do you think I should implement all of this? Keep in mind that at some point I might want to try and like persist some of the conversations to JSON. And so we can worry about that later. But for now, let's focus on just like this core multi-turn conversation ability."}